A||||7||DJWINNI||Simple question: How to now if the Turn Signal Flasher is out of order?||||1||
Z||000000||DJWINNI||12-14-2001||06:02 PM||||Hi!<BR> Could someone tell me how to know if the Turn Signal Flasher is out of order or not?<BR> In fact, my turn signals don't flash anymore. All my bulbs are good but I don't know if I've got to replace the fasher or not? I don't know, can it be tested? Can it be an other reason?<BR>Thanks!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||REDHOTT88||12-14-2001||06:09 PM||||<BR>I'm not sure how expensive flashers are in France, but the best way to test, is to replace!<P>However it sounds like you need a new flasher.<P><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Runs smooth, shifts crisp, red and shiny all over!)</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||12-15-2001||05:56 PM||||Do your 4 way flashers work? Or do none of your flashers work? I understand that you can swap the 4 way flasher can with the turn signal can to make them work.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||GTDude||12-15-2001||07:09 PM||||Do your lights burn bright when you turn the signal on right or left...but just will not blink?  If so..it is the flasher...definitely. It is located just under the panel under the steering wheel on a little clip.<P><P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||10
Z||000004||theogre||12-16-2001||12:06 AM||||Like they said above.... trade the one for the 4 ways to the turn signals. the flash rate may not be right but it will tell you if the can is the problem.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||DJWINNI||12-16-2001||08:58 AM||||Thanks for you answers,<BR>in fact, the lights just burn but don't flash. But the Hazzard lights flash. I've tried with the 4 ways one but It must be me who am a little bit bad with electricity! ;o)<BR>So, could someone tell me which terminals use? I mean, the flasher just has two terminals but the 4 ways one has more. Sorry for my ignorance!!<BR>Thanks <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://pageperso.aol.fr/djwinnimic/djwinnifierosignature.jpg"> ||||reg||5
Z||000006||GTDude||12-16-2001||11:05 AM||||The 4way flasher should be in the fuse panel and exactly like the turn flasher.  If you have more terminals you have the wrong thing.  Probably the horn relay.  It is round. Turn the 4ways on and feel the flasher on the fuse box you should feel it click.  Hope this helps.  Also, if the lights come on (all of the correct ones) then it is almost definitely the flasher.<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT<p>[This message has been edited by GTDude (edited 12-16-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||rogergarrison||12-16-2001||03:50 PM||||Just put in a new one. There only $2-$3. That most likely is your prob if they lite but dont blink. If you need anything from the wrecking yard, just grab a couple and pocket them, and some spare lite bulbs too <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
